cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ct-audit-action: constant-time RTL auditing on every pull request"
message: "If you use this in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: nickharris808
    website: "https://github.com/nickharris808"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickharris808/ct-audit-action"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nickh007/hw-verify-site"
abstract: >-
  A GitHub Action that runs a constant-time fan-in analysis over changed Verilog and
  reports leaks as annotations on the diff. Secrets are declared rather than inferred,
  so a file with none is skipped and reported as skipped. Files the analysis cannot
  read are counted separately from checked files and never rendered as constant-time,
  so an unanalysable file cannot quietly appear to pass review.
keywords:
  - continuous integration
  - constant-time
  - side-channel
  - hardware security
  - static analysis
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
